# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# NOTE: Cargo.lock is intentionally NOT ignored — ordeal ships a binary, so
# the lockfile is committed for reproducible builds.

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# cargo-fuzz artifacts and corpora
fuzz/target/
fuzz/corpus/
fuzz/artifacts/

# RustRover / JetBrains
#.idea/

# Nix
result
result-*
.direnv/

# Claude Code local settings (environment-specific)
.claude/settings.local.json
# Per-session, machine-local resume state: the pulseengine hooks rewrite this
# on every save, so it churns constantly and gets swept into unrelated commits.
**/.claude/pulseengine/working-context.md

# Rivet external project cache
.rivet/

# Bazel output symlinks
bazel-*
lean/.lake/

# TR-034 (issue #48): the Aeneas-generated Lean models are BUILD PRODUCTS —
# regenerated from the Rust sources by lean/regen.sh (locally) and by the
# Lean CI job (every run). Committing them would reintroduce the stale-model
# drift class the design retired. See docs/design/checker-single-sourcing.md.
lean/Kernel.lean
lean/BlastKernel.lean
